E — Open Questions for Formalisation

The following questions remain open and should be addressed when the Ontology formalisation layer is developed.
On Condition 3→4: The 八卦 借鉴 provides structural illumination but requires translation into a domain-independent formal condition. The precise definition of 'mutually constraining relations' that is both general enough to apply across all domains and specific enough to be empirically testable needs further work.
On Condition 5→6: The distinction between internally generated and externally attributed identity mapping needs a formal operationalisation that can be applied consistently across biological, social, and civilisational systems. The 釋層換名續存 category identified in the 漢儒整合 analysis may require its own formal treatment as a third continuation mode distinct from both genuine continuation and false continuation.
On the absorption problem: The six conditions falsify the state transitions. They do not yet fully resolve the absorption problem — the risk that a sufficiently general framework can reframe any counterexample as a lower-level special case. A complete resolution requires the framework to generate predictions about specific domains that could fail, not merely to describe those domains after the fact. This is the remaining work.
 
